{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQ5PTd9NvXxooqxFpxA7un","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t-        \"lane_status\": safe_status,\n151\t-    }\n152\t-    cleaned, dropped = _scrub_ceo_boot_event(\n153\t-        raw_event, _COUNCIL_LANE_INVOKED_ALLOWLIST\n154\t-    )\n155\t-    _write_event(cleaned)\n156\t-    if dropped:  # pragma: no cover — impossible from the typed wrapper\n157\t-        _breadcrumb(\n158\t-            f\"council_lane_invoked dropped forbidden field(s): \"\n159\t-            f\"{sorted(dropped)[:10]}\"\n160\t-        )\n161\t-\n162\t-\n163\t-def emit_codex_review_verdict(\n164\t-    *,\n165\t-    outcome: str,\n166\t-    diff_sha256: str = \"\",\n167\t-    session_id: str = \"\",\n168\t-    project: str = \"\",\n169\t-) -> None:\n170\t-    \"\"\"Emit codex_review_verdict (PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 liveness telemetry).\n171\t-\n172\t-    Fired by `codex_review_user_code.py` (the Stop-hook cross-model review of\n173\t-    the adopter's own risky diff) once per distinct (diff_sha256, outcome)\n174\t-    pair — the producer dedupes so Stop-retry loops re-review without\n175\t-    re-emitting. Closed outcome enum:\n176\t-\n177\t-      clean / findings     — a strictly PARSED verdict on a risky diff\n178\t-                             (the healthy class for the /ceo-boot\n179\t-                             `stop_review` liveness sub-rail)\n180\t-      skipped_failopen     — infra fail-open (codex missing / rc!=0 / empty\n181\t-                             stdout / timeout) OR a MALFORMED verdict; the\n182\t-                             coercion target for any unrecognized value\n183\t-      detected_only        — DETECT-ONLY default mode nudged a review but\n184\t-                             never ran one (neutral: never healthy, never\n185\t-                             failopen — r3 F3)\n186\t-\n187\t-    Deny-by-default field allowlist enforced: the ONLY caller fields are the\n188\t-    closed-enum `outcome`